From: Roman Rikhter <teledurak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw89: 8852ce: add RTL8832BR

The RTL8832BR (PCI 10ec:b832) is derived from the RTL8852C: its MAC,
baseband and PCIe blocks follow the RTL8852C, while the power on
sequence adds the LDO port and isolation steps of the RTL8852B. Add it
as a variant of the RTL8852CE with its own firmware and power on and
off sequences, and apply the PCIe settings the RTL8852C needs on its
first cut to all RTL8832BR cuts.

The power sequences follow the vendor driver for access points: the
chip does not enter SW LPS on power off, which a host that cannot wake
it again (such as the RTL8197F) sees as a device that stops answering.

Its firmware has no channel switch offload: it accepts scan offload
commands but stays on the current channel. Scan in software instead,
and keep the chip out of deep power save.

Its ADC runs at 960 MHz on the second cut and is trimmed per chip by
efuse values; set it up as the vendor driver does on every bandwidth
change, together with the DFIR type and tracking loop filters for
20 MHz, instead of the RTL8852C settings.

It is the 20/40/80 MHz product of its die: at 160 MHz it sends but
receives nothing. Leave 160 MHz out of its capabilities.

Signed-off-by: Roman Rikhter <teledurak@gmail.com>
---
diff --git drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.c drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.c
